WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.855
A country can grow richer

2
00:00:01.855 --> 00:00:04.195
without its people living better.

3
00:00:04.195 --> 00:00:05.618
That gap is why the

4
00:00:05.618 --> 00:00:08.268
Human Development Index exists.

5
00:00:08.606 --> 00:00:10.854
The UNDP published the first

6
00:00:10.854 --> 00:00:13.727
Human Development Report in 1990.

7
00:00:13.727 --> 00:00:15.105
It drew on the work

8
00:00:15.105 --> 00:00:16.544
of Mahbub ul Haq and

9
00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:17.919
Amartya Sen.

10
00:00:18.241 --> 00:00:19.900
A long and healthy life,

11
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.956
measured by life expectancy.

12
00:00:21.956 --> 00:00:24.109
Knowledge, through years of schooling.

13
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:25.572
And a decent standard of

14
00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:28.162
living, through income per person.

15
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:29.811
In GS3 answers,

16
00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:31.443
use it to separate growth

17
00:00:31.443 --> 00:00:32.814
from development.

18
00:00:32.814 --> 00:00:34.438
Growth is a means.

19
00:00:34.438 --> 00:00:37.048
Human development is the end.

20
00:00:37.721 --> 00:00:38.898
Your turn.

21
00:00:38.898 --> 00:00:41.448
Who publishes the H-D-I?
